title ALES1 — Lotus's audio byte stream: many frames reassembled into one gapless timeline
prompt recur the loop — take the next agent-doable Lindy-first crux-first lap, self-approve the design round, send each increment as its own signed round, stop at the custody gates
think ALES0 opened Season C with one framed buffer proven whole and sample-aligned. The road-on I named was the byte stream that carries many frames — the exact leap constel/channel.rye (FORA5) proved for the handshake. Agent-doable, no gate, bounded, high-confidence GREEN, directly continues the just-opened season. Lindy-first crux-first: a stream is the foundation every recorder and interface leans on before a timeline can edit anything.
think The crux beyond a generic byte channel is AUDIO-specific: ordered reassembly across frame boundaries. Two properties compose — delimiting (one whole frame at a time, NeedMoreBytes without moving the cursor, BadFrame on a wild length) and gapless in-order reassembly (drain every whole frame, lay its samples end to end so the timeline equals b0 ++ b1 ++ b2). Each frame is deframed verify-before-trust, so ALES0's two gates run per frame during reassembly — a torn-sample frame read cleanly by the delimiter still refuses PartialSample.
think Wrote lotus/stream.rye mirroring channel.rye's proven byte-FIFO shape (fixed buf, cursor, len, compact-on-drain), reusing the shared LOTS header (payload length at offset 6). Added a bounded Timeline (max 4*max_samples) and drain() that returns cleanly at NeedMoreBytes, propagates a real frame fault, and refuses TimelineFull. The stream only delimits and orders; it never re-checks a frame, so ALES0 stays the single trust boundary.
obs GREEN on the first build. Selftest proves: three frames back to back reassemble into b0 ++ b1 ++ b2 sample-for-sample and in order; a split frame refuses NeedMoreBytes without moving the cursor and completes on its last byte with no torn sample; a wild length refuses BadFrame before any over-read; an overfull stream refuses StreamFull; a torn-sample frame read cleanly by the delimiter still refuses PartialSample at the audio border during reassembly. TAME bans clean; ≥2 asserts/fn, u32 counts, i16 samples, copy loops not @memcpy, bounded drain guard. Purely local — no socket, no network, no keys, no funds, no real device; every custody gate untouched.
loom witness=ales_stream_witness wall_blocks=5 build=first_green max_stream_bytes=4180 max_timeline_samples=4096
